#uuid "1a37c432-ec3a-54fa-a265-be8a73e5b042" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260101} {:answer/id #uuid "570d06e5-402c-5a48-aa29-06ffa92a5243" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260619} {:answer/id #uuid "76d5eb3b-a067-51ff-b76b-ba5ac4fdd83a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260912} {:answer/id #uuid "bd179fed-e737-5b98-9f59-7194e6703cb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{9}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261544} {:answer/id #uuid "d688ed58-3493-5fc2-84fe-15f1d55d1e83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{18}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261762}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a37c432-ec3a-54fa-a265-be8a73e5b042" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260101} :answer-field/id #uuid "a12a44ba-4364-5ba9-9b64-63befc571bbb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262414}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "41f9cebe-1261-5298-9d1d-10bd7138212b" :question/math-academy-id "q-127609" :question/problem "If\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}3y & y \\\\ 3 & y-5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nand $det(A)=-27$, what is the value of $y?$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}3y & y \\\\ 3 & y-5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3y\\cdot (y-5)-y\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =3{y}^{2}-18y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(A)=-27$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =-27 \\\\ 3{y}^{2}-18y & =-27 \\\\ 3{y}^{2}-18y+27 & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2}-6y+9 & =0 \\\\ (y-3)^{2} & =0 \\\\ y & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292872 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "637424aa-e375-5ca5-bc92-9b93538da967" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291058}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "637424aa-e375-5ca5-bc92-9b93538da967" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291058} :answer-field/id #uuid "5deef2d0-b2e7-54ab-a3df-7734195f5705" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292019}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6d712990-6aa9-538b-af72-704fc59cbac8" :question/math-academy-id "q-275598" :question/problem "If\n$$\n\\displaystyle C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & k \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nand\n$\\text{det}(C)=-14,$ determine the value of $k.$\n\n$k=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(C) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & k \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot 6-k\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =6-4k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(C)=-14$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C) & =-14 \\\\ 6-4k & =-14 \\\\ -4k & =-14-6 \\\\ -4k & =-20 \\\\ k & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292873 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93399e4d-4d85-580e-9e08-c041fa5d5800" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291266}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93399e4d-4d85-580e-9e08-c041fa5d5800" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291266} :answer-field/id #uuid "339de4a9-ce7b-517d-9496-4255c739b1c2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291908}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d673c24b-03d4-55e8-a5fb-605bc1d6c21f" :question/math-academy-id "q-275601" :question/problem "If\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}3+p & 4p-{p}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 5-p\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nand $det(A)=7,$ what is the value of $p?$\n\n$p=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}3+p & 4p-{p}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 5-p\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(3+p)(5-p)-(4p-{p}^{2})\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =15-3p+5p-{p}^{2}-4p+{p}^{2} \\\\  & =15-2p-\\cancel{{p}^{2}}+\\cancel{{p}^{2}} \\\\  & =15-2p.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $det(A)=7$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =7 \\\\ 15-2p & =7 \\\\ -2p & =-8 \\\\ p & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299600 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d7fa1ff0-7dcd-55bd-a8fb-9db3d54aaf17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298479}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7fa1ff0-7dcd-55bd-a8fb-9db3d54aaf17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298479} :answer-field/id #uuid "154b6de9-0d77-5e77-8de1-45bf6ab48913" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298716}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1e3ffcd6-7f26-5f4f-8230-33ae44d7f744" :question/math-academy-id "q-317377" :question/problem "If\n$$\n\\displaystyle D=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & m \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nand\n$\\text{det}(D)=-11,$ determine the value of $m.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(D) & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & m \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 5-m\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =10-3m.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(D)=-11,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(D) & =-11 \\\\ 10-3m & =-11 \\\\ -3m & =-21 \\\\ m & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299601 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e2846b11-7ae8-5649-abfa-db38bcffb861" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298524}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e2846b11-7ae8-5649-abfa-db38bcffb861" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298524} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebf4f818-ea4f-5a3d-9526-388b53c60cf1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299436}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d0f61095-530a-54e2-bb79-353fa0efed39" :question/math-academy-id "q-317382" :question/problem "If\n$$\n\\displaystyle U=\\begin{bmatrix}1+r & 2-r \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nand $det(U)=-6$, what is the value of $r?$\n\n$r=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(U) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1+r & 2-r \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(1+r)\\cdot 4-(2-r)\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =4+4r+10-5r \\\\  & =14-r.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(U)=-6,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(U) & =-6 \\\\ 14-r & =-6 \\\\ -r & =-20 \\\\ r & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299602 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8cb2781e-f836-5ab8-a7a5-4a709b95dddb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298164}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8cb2781e-f836-5ab8-a7a5-4a709b95dddb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298164} :answer-field/id #uuid "0eda0fee-f95d-5630-8031-5abef3969057" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298688}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6e22859c-f056-5995-96a3-08af912796b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-317385" :question/problem "If\n$$\n\\displaystyle S=\\begin{bmatrix}3+s & 2s \\\\ -4 & 3-s\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nand $det(S)=25,$ what is the value of $s?$\n\n$s=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(S) & =\\begin{vmatrix}3+s & 2s \\\\ -4 & 3-s\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(3+s)(3-s)-2s(-4) \\\\  & =9-{s}^{2}+8s \\\\  & =-{s}^{2}+8s+9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(S)=25,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(S) & =25 \\\\ -{s}^{2}+8s+9 & =25 \\\\ -{s}^{2}+8s-16 & =0 \\\\ {s}^{2}-8s+16 & =0 \\\\ (s-4)^{2} & =0 \\\\ s & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335992 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bd1c86f-37e4-5b7b-9ec3-6d55d9670cea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333244} {:answer/id #uuid "4342bd65-1b39-56fb-b10b-45b1a8deeebc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333618} {:answer/id #uuid "982f2c1a-e0ab-57c2-b71f-62ccc2593e9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334339} {:answer/id #uuid "9e476a33-a9f4-5b54-ad86-0d592acad0c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334384} {:answer/id #uuid "ab173fd5-9f80-5b1f-9676-76188073a554" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334491}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e476a33-a9f4-5b54-ad86-0d592acad0c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334384} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c672b33-f965-56dc-b5e9-ce679a558195" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335509}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "66ad3ebb-398d-57e0-be2a-0ce7c08b87a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-69661" :question/problem "If\n$$\n\\displaystyle S=\\begin{bmatrix}1-p & 1+p \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nand $det(S)=2$, what is the value of $p?$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(S) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1-p & 1+p \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(1-p)\\cdot 2-(1+p)\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =2-2p+3+3p \\\\  & =5+p\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(S)=2$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(S) & =2 \\\\ 5+p & =2 \\\\ p & =2-5 \\\\ p & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186592241 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ec04919-851c-5f1c-955b-e2ff97fdf5f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186591815} {:answer/id #uuid "179118cd-8436-5fb0-9d7f-dcce778b3766" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186591825} {:answer/id #uuid "83672e87-80c5-5786-a4c9-02556e774a35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186591969} {:answer/id #uuid "e4fef352-25c1-5611-b453-4c7c29fa7623" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186592108} {:answer/id #uuid "e6683a70-94fb-5b5c-9555-12c8a50c3815" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186592110}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "179118cd-8436-5fb0-9d7f-dcce778b3766" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186591825} :answer-field/id #uuid "0de6d142-7706-50b2-ae89-6ca03ca1279e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186592155}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1de59b11-3c24-56b4-ab0a-82d3c06932c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-69658" :question/problem "If\n$$\n\\displaystyle U=\\begin{bmatrix}-v & 5 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nand\n$\\text{det}(U)=4$, what is the value of $v?$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(U) & =\\begin{vmatrix}-v & 5 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-v\\cdot 3-5\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-3v-20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(U)=4$, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(U) & =4 \\\\ -3v-20 & =4 \\\\ -3v & =4+20 \\\\ -3v & =24 \\\\ v & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186632688 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a492949-3bd3-5139-a09e-bd9913dab194" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632169} {:answer/id #uuid "60936ee6-077a-5769-8dc2-3c8fefce1f0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632286} {:answer/id #uuid "8ef20736-29c1-50f0-84a6-1558444988de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632364} {:answer/id #uuid "ca1c6019-99d5-5cac-a1f8-9077432f3728" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632446} {:answer/id #uuid "f70a2a78-ceac-54fe-b05a-31a8e59bf980" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632529}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca1c6019-99d5-5cac-a1f8-9077432f3728" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632446} :answer-field/id #uuid "10a75dfb-dbb7-5551-954d-06078da5405d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632550}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "67bf1af6-08b7-5d3a-b028-0c31c332e000" :question/math-academy-id "q-11647" :question/problem "If\n$$\n\\displaystyle B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & x \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nand\n$\\text{det}(B)=2$, what is the value of $x?$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(B) & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & x \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 6-x\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =12-2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $det(B)=2$, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =2 \\\\ 12-2x & =2 \\\\ -2x & =2-12 \\\\ -2x & =-10 \\\\ x & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186632702 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37d076a4-6367-5487-9f22-ea5c34784e3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632215}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37d076a4-6367-5487-9f22-ea5c34784e3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632215} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2f8f65c-9492-5e44-a731-352186ac01a7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186632623}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "948a413c-4dce-57f7-8b58-de4a73761168" :question/math-academy-id "q-275599" :question/problem "If\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}3+t & 4t \\\\ -3 & 3-t\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nand $det(A)=45,$ what is the value of $t?$\n\n$t=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}3+t & 4t \\\\ -3 & 3-t\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(3+t)(3-t)-4t(-3) \\\\  & =9-{t}^{2}+12t \\\\  & =-{t}^{2}+12t+9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(A)=45$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =45 \\\\ -{t}^{2}+12t+9 & =45 \\\\ -{t}^{2}+12t-36 & =0 \\\\ {t}^{2}-12t+36 & =0 \\\\ (t-6)^{2} & =0 \\\\ t & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186639317 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "005c827f-689c-5cf3-90d1-109920cf0783" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639312} {:answer/id #uuid "38a18f0f-2317-594f-8efd-6328ee622609" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639316} {:answer/id #uuid "6d2fbe70-79ba-5ce8-95da-6fd6fd50af02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639321} {:answer/id #uuid "e20fe210-3854-5d24-ac3a-84c2f2dfe577" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639334} {:answer/id #uuid "f300bc55-7ee3-5229-80ae-2b9eefd1c42e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639337}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f300bc55-7ee3-5229-80ae-2b9eefd1c42e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639337} :answer-field/id #uuid "71dbc4a4-c2ab-51eb-a362-49f13ff7f22c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639323}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4059a0e6-5992-5028-8c36-2765a1d37a20" :question/problem "If\n$$\n\\displaystyle U=\\begin{bmatrix}-3v & -7 \\\\ 8 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nand\n$\\text{det}(U)=-16$, what is the value of $v?$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(U) & =\\begin{vmatrix}-3v & -7 \\\\ 8 & -3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-3v)\\cdot (-3)-(-7)\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =9v+56\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(U)=-16$, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(U) & =-16 \\\\ 9v+56 & =-16 \\\\ 9v & =-16-56 \\\\ 9v & =-72 \\\\ v & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186639318 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fa9f658-ec24-5921-9904-29629964f774" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639314}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0fa9f658-ec24-5921-9904-29629964f774" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639314} :answer-field/id #uuid "bcd5acb9-fb09-5626-954d-96b09cf7d0cf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639332}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "46a646ff-1f4c-5382-ae10-f7d28464d45e" :question/problem "If\n$$\n\\displaystyle U=\\begin{bmatrix}-6-8r & 2-6r \\\\ 5 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nand $det(U)=182$, what is the value of $r?$\n\n$r=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(U) & =\\begin{vmatrix}-6-8r & 2-6r \\\\ 5 & 7\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-6-8r)\\cdot 7-(2-6r)\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-42-56r-10+30r \\\\  & =-52-26r.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(U)=182,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(U) & =182 \\\\ -52-26r & =182 \\\\ -26r & =234 \\\\ r & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186639325 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bdfc11ec-373d-57de-b54c-04933ee37f0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639333}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bdfc11ec-373d-57de-b54c-04933ee37f0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639333} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f65a0f8-1d0b-5f58-868d-246b5e15dc18" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639322}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7cea3e82-e2a1-50e4-a3dc-49d532c82f4a" :question/problem "If\n$$\n\\displaystyle C=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & k \\\\ -8 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nand\n$\\text{det}(C)=16,$ determine the value of $k.$\n\n$k=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(C) & =\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & k \\\\ -8 & -4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot (-4)-k\\cdot (-8) \\\\  & =8+8k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(C)=16$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C) & =16 \\\\ 8+8k & =16 \\\\ 8k & =16-8 \\\\ 8k & =8 \\\\ k & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186639327 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18c1b194-4820-510f-8ae8-e434621b24c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639315} {:answer/id #uuid "5f67fc68-3c45-5065-b1b1-022c24d47fd1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639319} {:answer/id #uuid "745bb945-f72e-581f-893e-68e5c56a6be3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639324} {:answer/id #uuid "ad1dc6a7-b788-5237-b036-89ce79c15958" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639330} {:answer/id #uuid "edfb9e4d-bf50-5404-9e1c-250542e45730" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639335}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f67fc68-3c45-5065-b1b1-022c24d47fd1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639319} :answer-field/id #uuid "83fd7816-cba8-5cfd-8cf1-72ff3b96cac5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639326}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "898c44e6-caae-5b89-a738-909dbdb2bd54" :question/problem "If\n$$\n\\displaystyle U=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -6 \\\\ -4k & 8k+2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nand\n$\\text{det}(U)=-6$, what is the value of $k?$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(U) & =\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & -6 \\\\ -4k & 8k+2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot (8k+2)-(-6)\\cdot (-4k) \\\\  & =-48k-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(U)=-6$, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(U) & =-6 \\\\ -48k-6 & =-6 \\\\ -48k & =-6-(-6) \\\\ -48k & =0 \\\\ k & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186639331 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01fccc5f-e11c-5381-8753-653378414177" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639313} {:answer/id #uuid "9f1a8e26-30e7-57f7-bb98-09c47d21b898" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639328} {:answer/id #uuid "a35ccc33-9c87-5d21-a82f-2f69c0c8c3ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639329} {:answer/id #uuid "f252b6de-fe64-5742-af1a-4b99b72662a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639336} {:answer/id #uuid "ff5daba2-9c57-556e-ab55-dad610664e28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639338}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f1a8e26-30e7-57f7-bb98-09c47d21b898" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639328} :answer-field/id #uuid "684879ec-f444-5c04-9846-f23446b2ed95" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639320}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b6541fe9-b31d-5be5-b2a6-4679896c9955" :question/problem "If\n$$\n\\displaystyle U=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 7 \\\\ 7k & 7k-5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nand\n$\\text{det}(U)=-89$, what is the value of $k?$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(U) & =\\begin{vmatrix}8 & 7 \\\\ 7k & 7k-5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =8\\cdot (7k-5)-7\\cdot 7k \\\\  & =7k-40\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(U)=-89$, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(U) & =-89 \\\\ 7k-40 & =-89 \\\\ 7k & =-89-(-40) \\\\ 7k & =-49 \\\\ k & =-7\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186639371 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0737dd86-7ea8-5edd-a7f6-9089c06e979b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639368}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0737dd86-7ea8-5edd-a7f6-9089c06e979b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639368} :answer-field/id #uuid "fdec6006-e422-576a-a0f7-8f139bc986c1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639379}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "38c47915-6f68-5518-b913-de4c53318abb" :question/problem "If\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}-5+p & -2p-{p}^{2} \\\\ 1 & -4-p\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nand $det(A)=38,$ what is the value of $p?$\n\n$p=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}-5+p & -2p-{p}^{2} \\\\ 1 & -4-p\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-5+p)(-4-p)-(-2p-{p}^{2})\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =20+5p-4p-{p}^{2}+2p+{p}^{2} \\\\  & =20+3p-\\cancel{{p}^{2}}+\\cancel{{p}^{2}} \\\\  & =20+3p.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $det(A)=38$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =38 \\\\ 20+3p & =38 \\\\ 3p & =18 \\\\ p & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186639375 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e8e32f0-f403-5921-a466-7f3d75d9c7bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639369}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e8e32f0-f403-5921-a466-7f3d75d9c7bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639369} :answer-field/id #uuid "83f455e3-cdd3-5426-bed7-c84613564549" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639376}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6e463122-efbb-5d02-95c5-fd1427b3ebb1" :question/problem "If\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}7+p & -6p-{p}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 2-p\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nand $det(A)=23,$ what is the value of $p?$\n\n$p=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}7+p & -6p-{p}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 2-p\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(7+p)(2-p)-(-6p-{p}^{2})\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =14-7p+2p-{p}^{2}+6p+{p}^{2} \\\\  & =14+p-\\cancel{{p}^{2}}+\\cancel{{p}^{2}} \\\\  & =14+p.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $det(A)=23$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =23 \\\\ 14+p & =23 \\\\ p & =9 \\\\ p & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186639377 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b918bc3-43cb-545f-b25b-277f6bf89403" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639374}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b918bc3-43cb-545f-b25b-277f6bf89403" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639374} :answer-field/id #uuid "327a7a0c-7023-5434-a7ce-ce3828aff719" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639370}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9333705c-58cc-567e-9660-11375155a969" :question/problem "If\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}4+p & 7p-{p}^{2} \\\\ 1 & -5-p\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nand $det(A)=-180,$ what is the value of $p?$\n\n$p=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}4+p & 7p-{p}^{2} \\\\ 1 & -5-p\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(4+p)(-5-p)-(7p-{p}^{2})\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-20-4p-5p-{p}^{2}-7p+{p}^{2} \\\\  & =-20-16p-\\cancel{{p}^{2}}+\\cancel{{p}^{2}} \\\\  & =-20-16p.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $det(A)=-180$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =-180 \\\\ -20-16p & =-180 \\\\ -16p & =-160 \\\\ p & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186639378 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64ad9141-f944-5052-ab08-7fd552b10459" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639373}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "64ad9141-f944-5052-ab08-7fd552b10459" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639373} :answer-field/id #uuid "63a925aa-d3fd-5dbc-95d4-49984cdf96ba" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186639372}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9de463d3-005b-5c57-8e51-9f4d98e4461a" :question/problem "If\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}3+p & 8p-{p}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 4-p\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nand $det(A)=82,$ what is the value of $p?$\n\n$p=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}3+p & 8p-{p}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 4-p\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(3+p)(4-p)-(8p-{p}^{2})\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =12-3p+4p-{p}^{2}-8p+{p}^{2} \\\\  & =12-7p-\\cancel{{p}^{2}}+\\cancel{{p}^{2}} \\\\  & =12-7p.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $det(A)=82$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =82 \\\\ 12-7p & =82 \\\\ -7p & =70 \\\\ p & =-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown in an Expression Involving the Determinant of a 2x2 Matrix"}]}
